⚖️ Legal Definition — Sovereign Steward

Sovereign Steward refers to a recognized, accountable custodian of sovereign intellectual property, data, or technological frameworks, who:

Exercises lawful custodianship over works or systems originating from their own authorship or trust (the “sovereign source”), and

Operates within the jurisdiction of existing national and international law — not apart from it.

It denotes sovereignty of authorship and origin, not political sovereignty or independence from government.
The Steward holds fiduciary, ethical, and legal responsibility to preserve, license, and enforce the integrity of those sovereign works under:

U.S. and international copyright law (e.g., 17 U.S.C. § 101 et seq.; Berne Convention)

Trade-secret and fiduciary doctrines

Contract and trust law, when the stewardship is formalized through corporate or fiduciary entities

