✅ Legal Position Summary

A Sovereign Steward retains moral and creative sovereignty over their works
while submitting to the jurisdiction of recognized law for protection and enforcement.

They may register, license, or assign rights under U.S. and global IP regimes.

They are not exempt from law; rather, they are empowered by it through rightful, documented ownership and governance fidelity.

In short:

A Sovereign Steward is the lawful custodian of self-originated intellectual property and governance systems — sovereign in authorship, but subject to and protected by recognized legal jurisdiction.
